/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// PHASE 2 — Studio MVP + Paid Features //
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
          DAYS 27-28: Copy self-hosted version → configure as hosted base + strip installer/multi-DB selector
          DAYS 29-30: Create frontend with login (3 auth layers: studio admin, tenant owner, end users)
          Days 31-32: Hosted storage layer
                      → nxt_data_* sharded tables (products, orders, posts, listings, comments, media, events, content)
                      → Storage resolver in DBAdapter (self-hosted real tables vs hosted nxt_data shards)
                      → Generated columns + expression indexes for hot fields
                      → Postgres RLS policies + tenant isolation middleware
          Days 33-34: Redis + BullMQ infrastructure
                      → Redis: tenant config cache, model schema cache, auth cache, hot-read cache, quota counters
                      → BullMQ: webhook delivery, email, code gen jobs, analytics aggregation, exports, backups
                      → Workers: separate process, queue consumers
          Days 35-37: Studio admin panel — accounts, billing, plans, usage, license keys, tenant suspension, audit log
          Days 38-39: Teams & permissions
                      → nxt_accounts + nxt_account_members tables
                      → nxt_project_members with role-based access
                      → Invite flow with email
                      → Role-based middleware on every API
                      → Team UI + project member management
          Days 40–41: Wire self-hosted to Studio — license validation (signed JWT), phone home (24h cadence), 
                      revocation list, usage tracking, offline grace period
          Days 42–44: Integrations — category tabs, connect/disconnect, OAuth flows, webhook support
          Days 45–47: API Builder + complete public API endpoints
                      → Custom endpoint creation, business logic editor, test panel
                      → Auth middleware, query params for filtering, write endpoints
                      → Default CRUD-per-model gateway with rate limiting per tenant
          Days 48–50: Page Builder — drag and drop components, layout system, preview, publish — Studio version only
          Days 51–53: Flutter code generation — models, pages, navigation
                      → Client/end-user auth flow for generated app (signin/signup/forgot/reset)
                      → App navigation system (nxf_menus with app_target: cms | flutter | nextjs)
          Days 54–56: Next.js code generation — models, pages, API routes
                      → Client/end-user auth flow for generated app
                      → App navigation system reused from Flutter target
          Days 57–58: Code generation testing — generate sample apps, fix issues
          Day  59:    Switch between self-hosted and hosted with API keys
          Days 60–62: Help center — structure, categories, core articles
          Days 63–65: Developer docs — API reference, adapter docs, deployment guide
          Days 66–68: End to end QA — self-hosted flow, hosted flow, license checks, all DB types, RLS leakage tests
          Days 69–75: Buffer — spillover, bug fixes, polish, translate all messages JSON

///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// ARCHITECTURE DECISIONS THAT NEED ATTENTION //
// (Research required — pick before Day 27) //
///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

// 1. DOMAIN & DEPLOYMENT
//    - Studio domain: studio.<rebrand>.com vs other subdomain?
//    - Tenant URLs: subdomains (acme.<rebrand>.app) vs path-based?
//    - Hosting: Render vs Railway vs Vercel vs own VPS?
//    - SSL: Cloudflare in front vs host-managed only?

// 2. DATABASE
//    - Postgres provider: Neon vs Supabase vs Render vs RDS vs self-managed?
//    - Single region vs multi-region from start?
//    - Backup strategy: provider PITR vs own pg_dump cron vs both?

// 3. AUTH (3 LAYERS)
//    - Studio admins — separate table, 2FA required?
//    - Tenant owners — existing nxf_users schema
//    - End users of generated apps — per-tenant JWT secrets?
//    - Token format and refresh strategy for each layer

// 4. BILLING
//    - Provider: Stripe vs Paddle vs Lemon Squeezy (ZA → global = tax implications)
//    - Pricing model: flat tiers vs usage-based vs hybrid?
//    - What to meter: API calls / storage / projects / apps / models?
//    - Free tier limits — generous enough to try, tight enough to convert?

// 5. TENANT ISOLATION
//    - App middleware (withTenant helper) + Postgres RLS combo?
//    - RLS policy structure
//    - Cross-tenant leakage test suite

// 6. LICENCE KEY
//    - Generate on subscription webhook?
//    - Format: signed JWT vs random string?
//    - Revocation strategy and list distribution
//    - Phone-home cadence (24h?) and offline grace period (7d soft, 30d hard?)

// 7. PLAN LIMITS & ENFORCEMENT
//    - Where to enforce: UI / API gateway / both?
//    - Soft warnings at 80%, hard stop at 100%?
//    - Quota counters in Redis with Postgres sync?

// 8. ONBOARDING EMAILS
//    - Provider: Resend vs Postmark vs SendGrid?
//    - Minimum email set: welcome, payment failed, cancelled, quota warning
//    - Template system (React Email)?

// 9. OBSERVABILITY
//    - Error tracking: Sentry vs alternatives
//    - Logs + uptime + status page: BetterStack vs stitched vendors
//    - Product analytics: Posthog vs Mixpanel vs none
//    - Per-tenant analytics dashboard for internal use

// 10. SUPPORT CHANNEL
//    - Email-only at launch (which inbox?) — upgrade to Helpscout later?
//    - Status page provider — BetterStack vs instatus vs other

// 11. LEGAL / COMPLIANCE
//    - ToS + Privacy + Cookie + DPA — Termly vs iubenda vs lawyer?
//    - POPIA registration (free SA Information Regulator)
//    - AUP — what tenants can't do on infra
//    - Cookie banner on marketing site

// 12. MARKETING SITE
//    - Separate repo, runs on root domain
//    - Pages: home / pricing / comparison / docs link / blog / login
//    - Sandbox demo login — yes/no?

// 13. SELF-HOSTED ↔ STUDIO COMMUNICATION
//    - What data goes back (anonymised usage only — be transparent)
//    - Public doc page listing exactly what's sent
//    - Offline grace period definition

// 14. DATA EXPORT (GDPR)
//    - Format: ZIP with project.json, models.json, data/, media/?
//    - Trigger: button → queued job → emailed S3 link?
//    - Streaming during export for big tenants

// 15. KILLSWITCH / ABUSE
//    - Suspend account flow (manual at launch)
//    - Audit trail of admin actions
//    - Refund/credit logic via billing provider

